      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "The domain of the goal (e.g. revenue vs satisfaction) plausibly influences both which management practices are adopted and baseline achievement rates, acting as a common cause. Not named in the query."
    },
    {
      "name": "management_lever_type",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": true,
      "rationale": "Represents the type of goal-management practice/lever adopted -- an intervenable action an actor could set or choose. This is the treatment implied by 'adopting the practices'."
    },
    {
      "name": "target_improvement_magnitude",
      "causal_role": "other",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Encodes the target/expected improvement size; this is closer to a restatement of the outcome ambition than a common cause. Not a confounder."
    },
    {
      "name": "mechanism_type",
      "causal_role": "mediator",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "The mechanism through which the practice operates lies on the causal path from treatment to outcome, so it is a mediator, not a confounder."
    },
    {
      "name": "quantified_specificity",
      "causal_role": "other",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Whether the practice is quantified is a property of the practice description; constant (all true) so carries no adjustment value."
    },
    {
      "name": "baseline_context_provided",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Whether a baseline was provided can affect both how a practice is framed/adopted and measured achievement, plausibly a common cause. Weakly so."
    },
    {
      "name": "has_feedback_loop",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "A configurable design property of the practice that could be set/changed; functions as an intervenable feature rather than a confounder."
    },
    {
      "name": "involves_stakeholder_engagement",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Another settable design feature of the practice, part of the treatment bundle rather than a common cause."
    },
    {
      "name": "implementation_feasibility_signal",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Implementation barriers affect both whether/how a practice is adopted and the achievable completion, a plausible common cause to adjust for. Not named in query."
    },
    {
      "name": "implementation_scope",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Scope of implementation influences both which practices are chosen and achievement outcomes; plausible common cause not named in the query."
    },
    {
      "name": "outcome_metric_type",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "The type of metric conditions how percent_complete is measured and correlates with domain/practice choice; a plausible common cause. Not named in query."
    }
  ],
  "treatment_present": true,
  "treatment_columns": ["management_lever_type", "has_feedback_loop", "involves_stakeholder_engagement"],
  "treatment_intervenable": true,
  "confounders": [
    {"name": "goal_domain", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.6},
    {"name": "baseline_context_provided", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.4},
    {"name": "implementation_feasibility_signal", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.6},
    {"name": "implementation_scope", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.6},
    {"name": "outcome_metric_type", "named_in_query": false, "plausibility": 0.5}
  ],
  "confounder_quality": 0.55,
  "rationale": "The added columns clearly establish an intervenable treatment: goal-management practice characteristics (lever type, feedback loop, stakeholder engagement) are things actors can actually set or change, satisfying condition (a). Several columns also serve as genuine confounders -- common causes of both practice adoption and achievement -- none of which were named in the query (goal_domain, implementation_feasibility, implementation_scope, outcome_metric_type), which demonstrates the capability under test. However, the set is diluted by a mediator (mechanism_type), a near-restatement of the outcome (target_improvement_magnitude), and a constant, non-informative column (quantified_specificity). The confounders are plausible but individually of moderate strength and the treatment/confounder distinction is somewhat blurred, so overall confounder quality is moderate rather than strong."
}
